 🎨 If you are looking for inspiration, you can check [MUI Treasury's customization examples](https://mui-treasury.com/primitive/text-field).
 
+### Custom variants
+
+In addition to the built-in `outlined`, `filled`, and `standard` variants, you can add your own variant using the theme's `variants` key:
+
+```js
+const theme = createTheme({
+  components: {
+    MuiTextField: {
+      variants: [
+        {
+          props: { variant: 'dashed' },
+          style: {
+            '& .MuiOutlinedInput-notchedOutline': {
+              borderStyle: 'dashed',
+            },
+          },
+        },
+      ],
+    },
+  },
+});
+```
+
+If you're using TypeScript, you'll need to declare the new variant using [module augmentation](https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/declaration-merging.html#module-augmentation):
+
+```tsx
+declare module '@mui/material/TextField' {
+  interface TextFieldPropsVariantOverrides {
+    dashed: true;
+  }
+}
+```
+
+A custom variant renders the [`OutlinedInput`](/material-ui/api/outlined-input/) component and never notches its outline for the label.
+Pass `slots.input` if you need it to render a different input component.
+
 ## `useFormControl`
 
 For advanced customization use cases, a `useFormControl()` hook is exposed.
